    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / LD_PRELOAD Hook Source Drop", "technique": "T1574.006", "what_happened": "At 2030-02-18 09:42:08 CET, Wazuh FIM on linux-app-srv-31 (agent.id=131) reported syscheck.event='added' on syscheck.path='/tmp/p81_hook_20300218_094208.c' (uname_after=jbar uid=1006). Content (via diff): C source that hooks getuid(), geteuid(), getgid(), getegid() to return 0 — overriding the dynamic linker's UID lookup so any binary sees uid=0.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 80700 'FIM .c file with getuid hook content' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1574.006."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Compile Hook Shared Object", "technique": "T1574.006", "what_happened": "At 09:42:12, auditd captured: data.audit.exe='/usr/bin/gcc', data.audit.command='gcc -shared -fPIC -nostartfiles -o /tmp/p81_hook_20300218_094208.so /tmp/p81_hook_20300218_094208.c -ldl', data.audit.uid=1006. The flags '-shared -fPIC -nostartfiles' build a shared library that can be LD_PRELOAD'd. FIM then captured the resulting .so file creation.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 554 'new .so in /tmp' + rule 80701 'gcc -shared in /tmp by non-root' fired."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "LD_PRELOAD Execution", "technique": "T1574.006", "what_happened": "At 09:42:18, auditd captured: data.audit.exe='/usr/bin/id', data.audit.command='id', data.audit.uid=1006. CRITICALLY, the proc info captured by auditd's env-capture shows the process environment included 'LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/p81_hook_20300218_094208.so'. The 'id' output was 'uid=0(root) gid=0(root) groups=0(root)' — the hook successfully tricked id into reporting root.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 100200 'LD_PRELOAD set in process env before execve from writable path' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1574.006."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Privilege Escalation via Setuid Binary + LD_PRELOAD", "technique": "T1574.006", "what_happened": "At 09:43:42, jbar attempted the FULL escalation: 'LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/p81_hook_20300218_094208.so /usr/bin/sudo bash'. While modern sudo strips LD_PRELOAD via secure_getenv(), some setuid binaries on this host (an older custom 'corp_admin_tool' utility) do NOT strip it. auditd captured: data.audit.exe='/usr/local/bin/corp_admin_tool' (SUID-root), data.audit.uid=1006 but data.audit.euid=0 — the binary ran with root euid AND with the malicious LD_PRELOAD active. The corp_admin_tool spawned bash; root shell achieved.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 100201 'SUID binary execve with LD_PRELOAD set from writable path' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1574.006."}
